# ============================================================================
# Default build-context filter (repository root)
# ============================================================================
# Both images build from the repo root because the pnpm workspace lockfile
# lives here. BuildKit prefers the more specific `backend/Dockerfile.dockerignore`
# and `frontend/Dockerfile.dockerignore`; this file is the fallback and the
# baseline for any ad-hoc `docker build .`.
# ============================================================================

# --- version control & CI ---------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# --- editors / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- dependency trees & build output (always rebuilt inside the image) ------
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
.pnpm-store

# --- secrets and local state (must NEVER enter an image layer) --------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
secrets
**/logs
**/*.log
.deploy.lock

# --- data & backups ---------------------------------------------------------
mongo-backups
redis-backups
letsencrypt
caddy_data

# --- docs, design assets and scripts ----------------------------------------
docs
design
*.md
LICENSE
CITATION.cff

# --- compose/infra files (mounted at runtime, not built in) -----------------
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yaml
Caddyfile
.trivyignore
